I'm pretty fond of Mojo too, don't get me wrong, but I don't know
anymore.  I got to liking Excalibur in my recent game (ascended an elf,
but got sick of stormbringer so went for the helm of opp alignment +
longsword + fountain = excalibur deal).  The real great thing about
excalibur (and stormy) is the protection from level drain, i really got
to liking that.  The real beauty of excalibur is the ease with which
you can attain it.  

Vorpal Blade can be a real lifesaver when you are fighting the wiz
or something like that that teleports away to heal; eventually you just
behead it; no more problem.

The Tusurugi of murmasa is OK for this too, but you can't wear a
shield, so the only way to get reflection is an amulet, and reflection
is a must.  Therefore no amulet of life saving.  therefore the ToM is a
downer.

As above, stormbringer pisses me off with the stupid "attack everything"
business.  It spent the latter 3/4 of my game in a chest.  

Grayswandir can't be beat when you're fighting demons; the silver damage
plus the artifact bonus is a real sweet deal.  It will do more damage than
mjollnir to silver-haters.  

I like frost and fire brand a lot too, and Magicbane is certainly nothing
to be sneezed at.  

Cleaver kinda sucks because, as the ToM, it is two-handed.  

Some of the quest artifact weapons have cool effects, like regeneration
and such, so they can be useful.

My big downers are:
 Sting/Orcrist  (except that you can make them by naming)
 Anything-Slayer
 Anything-Bane except magicbane
 SunSword
 Ogresmasher

I guess my overall favorite has to be Vorpal Blade, but I'm really 
attached to a lot of the other weapons. 

